m"},{"content_hash":"5c3a5848e21d1e5c00d90c78a75b31a4b20094fa19be3b692fb6c9ceddb581a5","event_uuid":"bf928440-1490-42e9-a9d7-12065db06dad","position":{"commit_sha":"be97c9b7ef0ca06397469b768a0249fb4766fb12","position":"1785451640521243001-bf928440-1490-42e9-a9d7-12065db06dad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"985c3b7d-a16c-4dad-8e79-94df7d806053","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Possibly relevant field evidence from an AWS CloudTrail audit (2026-07-30), offered as data rather than a diagnosis.\n\nAmong today's `bedrock:Converse` calls, four failed within a single second with a model-identifier error distinct from the parameter-deprecation errors that bug 1903 covers:\n\n    2026-07-30T20:34:23Z  ValidationException: The provided model identifier is invalid.   (x4)\n    2026-07-30T16:03:39Z  ValidationException: Invocation of model ID anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n                          with on-demand throughput isn't supported. Retry your request with the\n                          ID or ARN of an inference profile.\n\nWhy this may bear on this ticket: if `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` is parsed and documented but read by nothing, then whatever id actually reaches `Converse` comes from another source, and these are the observable symptoms of the id that is really being sent. The 16:03:39Z line in particular shows a bare foundation-model id being used where an inference-profile id is required.\n\nI have NOT traced these calls to a specific code path and cannot confirm they originate from the unread config key — they were made under `user/joe_frontier` during interactive Bedrock work, so they may equally be manual experimentation. Treat as a lead to confirm or dismiss, not as evidence of the defect.\n\nCross-ref: 1903 (temperature/top_p override table), 9249 (instance-role Bedrock access).","timestamp":1785451640521243001}],"created_at":1785435490210394001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"57800c27-7610-4b11-b797-061a02b38654","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2932-8a98-6d70-4550"},{"link_uuid":"9918a47a-ab04-409d-b950-1c7676d3ae23","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0902-cb7a-c23e-4f86"}],"description":"# Remove the inert `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` / `bedrock_model_id` config knob\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStory S3 [rebar:2932-8a98-6d70-4550] landed a `bedrock_model_id` field on `LLMConfig`\n(`src/rebar/llm/config.py:521`), populated it from `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` and the\n`[tool.rebar.llm] bedrock_model_id` table key (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:633-638`), described it in the\nmodule docstring (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:21-22`), listed it in `docs/env-vars.md:55`, and duplicated its\ndefault literal into `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py:38` behind a hand-sync comment.\n\n**Nothing reads it.** A grep across `src/` and `tests/` finds no consumer other than the dataclass field\ndeclaration and the `from_env` assignment that populates it. The Bedrock model id is in fact carried by\n`cfg.model` as the provider-prefixed string `bedrock:<inference-profile-id>` — `providers.py` parses the\nprovider from that prefix, and that is the path S3's own tests exercise.\n\nSo an operator who sets `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` gets **silence**: no model change, no warning, no\nerror, and a documented env var that does nothing. This was found while checking whether the field could\nserve as a second model knob for the per-pass model requirement recorded on\n[rebar:eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a]; it cannot, because it is not wired at all.\n\n**It has never shipped.** Change 1043 (which introduced it) is unsubmitted, so the defect exists only\ninside the in-flight epic stack and can mislead no operator until that stack lands. This ticket removes it\nbefore it ever does.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Delete the knob** — the field, the `from_env` wiring, the two docstring lines, the `docs/env-vars.md`\nrow, and the duplicated literal in `bedrock_model.py` (which then needs no hand-sync comment, since the\nsole remaining definition is the one `bedrock_model.py` itself owns).\n\nDeletion over wiring, for three reasons:\n\n1. `cfg.model` ALREADY carries the Bedrock model id, and that is the tested, working path. Wiring a second\n   knob means inventing precedence rules between two ways to express one value — a config ambiguity that\n   would then need its own tests and documentation.\n2. Nothing depends on it. Because it never shipped, removal is not a compatibility change: no configuration\n   that works today stops working, since no configuration using it works today.\n3. It does not serve the per-pass model work it was investigated for. That needs a per-pass MAPPING\n   (Pass-1 vs Pass-2/Pass-4); a single scalar cannot express one, so keeping the field \"in case\" buys\n   nothing concrete.\n\n**Alternative rejected — wire it up so the documented knob works.** This adds a redundant second path to a\nvalue `cfg.model` already carries, requires precedence rules against the provider-prefixed form, and\nenlarges the config surface to satisfy documentation that is itself the thing in error. Fixing the docs by\ndeleting the row is strictly smaller than fixing the code to match the docs.\n\n**Alternative rejected — amend change 1043 so the field never appears in history.** Cleaner history, but\n1043 already holds `LLM-Review +1`; amending resets that vote and forces a re-review, delaying S3's close\non the epic's critical path. Because the whole stack submits together, main's landed state is identical\neither way.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — remove the `bedrock_model_id` field (`:521`), its `from_env` population\n  (`:633-638`), and its module-docstring lines (`:21-22`).\n- `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py` — drop the \"duplicated ... kept in sync by hand\" rationale now that\n  `config.py` no longer holds a second copy; `DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` itself STAYS (it is the live\n  default this module documents as measured-working).\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — remove the `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` row (`:55`).\n- `tests/unit/` — the regression test below.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier: the mechanism is config parsing, which is pure and in-process — no model call, no AWS.\n\n- **regression (the actual defect):** setting `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` in the environment does not\n  silently produce a config that claims a Bedrock model id — asserting `LLMConfig.from_env()` exposes no\n  `bedrock_model_id` attribute, so a future reintroduction of an unread field fails this test.\n- **collateral invariant:** the working path is untouched — a `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=bedrock:us.anthropic.\n  claude-sonnet-4-6` config still resolves provider `bedrock` and that model id through `providers.py`.\n- **docs/code agreement:** no `REBAR_LLM_*` name documented in `docs/env-vars.md` is absent from\n  `config.py` (guards the general class of defect, not just this instance), if that check is cheap enough\n  to be reliable; otherwise assert the specific name is gone from both.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `grep -r bedrock_model_id src/ docs/` returns only `bedrock_model.py`'s own\n      `DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` definition and its docstring\n- [ ] a test asserts `LLMConfig.from_env()` has no `bedrock_model_id` attribute when\n      `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` is set in the environment\n- [ ] a test asserts `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=bedrock:<profile-id>` still resolves the bedrock provider and that\n      model id (the working path is not collateral damage)\n- [ ] `docs/env-vars.md` no longer lists `REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID`","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0902-cb7a-c23e-4f86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c07c574a-2d28-4041-8a85-a1c3095e735f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"281f-3336-c668-4979","ticket_type":"bug","title":"REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID is parsed and documented but read by nothing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1f0afc8a-41f7-48d1-a52c-b6840e8686ce","57800c27-7610-4b11-b797-061a02b38654","baa7ae8e-66bb-43be-b2b0-941c1625c964","9b3592eb-6529-4101-a8ee-d4dfccb3dc5c","c07c574a-2d28-4041-8a85-a1c3095e735f","57e9885d-af71-4e21-8c02-3630e89e2235","f74544cf-ee9c-4c21-aaf0-958d85821a07","c1cf0907-bfcb-4822-b2a4-a1e000cc4c60","bf928440-1490-42e9-a9d7-12065db06dad","9918a47a-ab04-409d-b950-1c7676d3ae23"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785453552436396179,"uuid":"814621bb-13cc-406e-a2ea-a60503068938"}